# SIMULATION (model curve), NOT an observation. Cain et al. (2025), ApJ 980, 83 (arXiv:2409.02989), Fig. 1 top (red dashed): x_HI = 1 - x_HII^V, the volume-averaged ionized fraction (linear axis).
#   "early start/late end" model: follows Munoz+24 at z >= 10, then drops to match the forest;
#   midpoint z ~ 7.5, reionization ends at z ~ 5; photon budget 2.8 per H atom.
#   FlexRT ray-tracing radiative transfer (200 cMpc/h) with sub-grid sinks; Ndot(z) is an INPUT built from the JWST-era UV
#   luminosity density times an assumed <f_esc xi_ion>, and matched to the mean Lya transmission of Bosman et al. (2022; XQR-30)
#   at z <= 6; h = 0.68. Not the same paper as Cain2025 (the PASA emissivity measurement).
#   Read from the published RASTER figure (pixel-traced, ~1 px uncertainty; curve hidden under other lines left as gaps);
#   curve: Cain2025_2409.02989/extracted/Cain2025_Fig1_xHI_EarlyStartLateEnd.csv in the papers folder.
#   Rows with x_HI < 0.001 are dropped: the linear x_ion axis does not resolve them.
